  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "Following the vacancy of the vice presidential office, President Prabowo Subianto is evaluating potential candidates to succeed Gibran Rakabuming Raka. While names such as Andi Amran Sulaiman and Sugiono have surfaced as prominent contenders, Sufmi Dasco, a key political figure, has publicly stated that he is not interested in the position. Dasco noted that he was personally tasked by the President to provide a list of two suitable candidates for consideration. Concurrently, the selection process has invited discussions regarding the legal framework for replacing a vice president mid-term. Academic and legal observers have expressed concerns that the current 60-day mandate for appointing a successor is administratively complex. The ongoing deliberation considers various factors, including political loyalty and policy execution capabilities, while public scrutiny has extended to the background and tax status of the leading candidates under review by the administration.",
